# Exclude build scratch from the Pages asset set.
#
# pages_build_output_dir is "." (the repo root), so wrangler writes its esbuild
# scratch to .wrangler/tmp INSIDE the directory being served. The asset watcher
# then sees wrangler's own scratch as a change and rebuilds, which writes more
# scratch, which triggers another rebuild. That loop is why local responses
# sometimes took four minutes and why the dev server would die under memory
# pressure.
#
# --persist-to moves the state/cache out of the project, but it does not move
# .wrangler/tmp, so the loop still happens. Ignoring the directory stops the
# watcher from ever seeing it.
#
# Everything else here is deliberately NOT ignored: the site really is served
# from the repo root, so functions/, migrations/ and the artwork are all part of
# the upload the way they are today.
.wrangler/
